      "recommendation": "Before any migration, freeze a minimal real original\u2192export\u2192reimport fixture with two distinct source-versioned node identities and one typed edge. Require exact endpoint namespace/identity/role/ordinal preservation, referential closure and complete counts; empty/missing/foreign endpoints must produce an explicit unresolved/refused disposition rather than an empty-string successful edge. Then test the current faulty projection and correction on a bounded pinned legacy sample before a complete indexed rebuild. Do not assume the upstream original field names or primary-graph namespace without inspecting its producer.",
      "severity": "minor",
      "topic": "Make first exporter regression explicit"
